  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve for $z$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+z & =2\\,\u27f9\\,z=2-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+(2-x)^{2} & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+(4-4x+{x}^{2}) & =4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x+4+(y+1)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4x+4+(y+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x+2+(y+1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x+1)+(y+1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2}=1.$",
